$DATUM (2S,4S) -tert-Butyl 2-(Hex-5-en-1-yl(methyl)-carbamoyl) -4-((7-m e t hox
y -8-m e t h y l -2 -(4
-(trifluoromethyl)thiazol-2-yl)quinolin-4-yl)oxy)-pyrrolidine-1-carboxylate
(28). Acid 27 (92% w/w, 21.33 g, 35.6 mmol) was dissolved in DMF (49 mL)
and O-(benzotriazol-1-yl)-N,N, N′, N′-tetramethyluronium
tetrafluoroborate (14.74 g, 44.5 mmol) was charged in one portion at 20-
25 °C. After 10 min, N-methylhex-5-en-1-amine tosylate 7 (11.18 g, 39.2
mmol) was charged to the mixture in one portion. The mixture was cooled
to 5-10 °C and N,N-diisopropylethylamine (18.72 mL, 106.92 mmol) was
charged over 10 minutes. The mixture was warmed to 20-25 °C and monitored
by HPLC. After 1 h, EtOAc (180 mL) was added followed by NaCl (aq,
saturated, 200 mL). The layers were separated and the aqueous phase was
extracted with EtOAc (90 mL). The combined organic layers were washed
with NH4Cl (aq, 5% w/w, 3 × 200 mL) and NaCl (aq, half saturated, 120
mL), dried using anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and distilled under vacuum at
40-45 °C. The residue was chased with TBME/n-heptane 4:1 (60 mL) to give
crude amide 28 (23.94 g). The crude material was digested with EtOAc (24
mL) and n-heptane (115 mL) was added over 15 min at 20- 25 °C, producing
a white precipitate. The slurry was stirred for 30 min and then filtered
and the resulting solids were rinsed with EtOAc/n-heptane 1:5 (2 × 6 mL)
and dried under vacuum at 40-45 °C to give amide 28. off-white powder
(20.8 g, 90% yield, &gt;99% LCAP at 254 nm). HPLC (Method A): tR 8.38
minutes. Mp: 158 °C. [α]D25 -5.5 (c 1.0, CHCl3). MS (ESI+) m/z: 649.22 [M
+ H]+, 1297.61 [2M + H] +. IR (KBr disc, cm-1) νmax: 2936, 1708, 1642,
1610. 1H NMR δH (400 MHz, d6-DMSO, mixture of rotamers): 1.04-1.48 (4H,
6m, H-20, H-20a, H-19, H-19a), 1.33, 1.40, 1.41 (9H, 3s, C(CH3)3),
1.66-2.04 (2H, 3m, H-21, H-21a), 2.09-2.13 (1H, m, H-3a), 2.54 (3H, s,
CH3), 2.74, 2.78, 2.89, 2.92 (3H, 4s, NCH3), 2.83- 3.24 (3H, 5m, H-3,
H-18, H-18a), 3.24-3.35 (1H, m, H-5a), 3.94-4.00 (4H, m, H-5, OCH3),
4.66-5.00 (3H, m, H-2, H-23, H-23a), 5.50-5.57 (1H, m, H-4), 5.60-5.75
(1H, m, H-22), 7.38-7.46 (2H, m, H-7, H-10), 7.94-7.98 (1H, m, H-9), 8.64
(1H, s, H-17). 13C NMR δC (100 MHz, d6-DMSO, mixture of rotamers): 9.68
(CH3), 25.03, 25.37 (C-20), 25.96, 26.09, 27.27 (C-19), 27.86, 27.98,
28.09 (C(CH3)3), 32.77, 32.90 (C-21), 33.17, 34.12, 34.30 (NCH3), 35.36,
36.25 (C-3), 46.79, 47.07, 48.10 (C-18), 52.04, 52.39 (C-5), 56.04
(OCH3), 56.36 (C-2), 75.13, 75.28 (C-4), 78.52, 78.69, 78.82 (C(CH3)3),
94.70 (C-7), 113.02, 113.15, 113.28 (C-10), 114.56, 114.67, 114.93
(C-23), 116.32 (C-14), 119.87 (C-12), 120.44 (1C, q, 1JC-F 268.5 Hz,
CF3), 121.15 (C-9), 126.47 (C-17), 138.34, 138.38 (C-22), 143.51 (1C, q,
2JC-F 36.3 Hz, C-16), 147.63 (C-13), 149.64 (C-6), 153.09, 153.17 (NCOO),
158.16 (C-11), 160.86 (C-8), 170.25, 170.35 (CONMe), 172.47 (C-15). 19F
NMR δF (376 MHz, d6-DMSO, mixture of rotamers): -62.30, -62.31 (3F, 2s,
CF3). Anal. Calcd for C32H39F3N4O5S: C, 59.24; H, 6.06; N, 8.64; F, 8.79;
S, 4.94. Found: C, 59.34; H, 6.42; N, 8.69; F, 8.75; S, 5.05.
