$DATUM Compound (E)-36. Compound (E)-33 (442 mg, 2.14 mmol) and oxadiazole 30
(492 mg, 1.43 mmol) were dissolved in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (14 mL). EDCI (410
mg, 2.14 mmol) and DMAP (262 mg, 2.14 mmol) were added to the resulting
solution, which was then stirred for 16 h at room temperature. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue was purified
by flash chromatography (SiO2, 30% EtOAc-hexanes) to afford 36. Yield 674
mg, 89%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.39-7.27 (m, 6H), 6.78-6.73 (m, 3H),
6.42 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 1H), 4.89 (dt, J = 12.6, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 4.70 (s, 2H),
4.08-4.07 (m, 2H), 4.05 (s, 3H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 3.68 (s, 3H), 2.84-2.77
(m, 4H), 2.32 (q, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 2.11-2.07 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 171.6, 162.0, 156.3, 154.1, 153.5, 147.2, 137.7, 136.9, 128.4
(2C), 127.8, 127.5 (2C), 124.8, 122.0, 119.3, 113.2, 108.5, 102.5, 92.8,
71.0, 55.6, 53.6, 46.9, 37.4, 32.5, 28.1, 23.3, 22.1; IR (film) νmax
2944, 1745, 1706, 1563, 1440, 1153, 813, 734 cm-1; HRMS ESI-TOF m/z
533.2403 (C29H32N4O6 + H+ requires 533.2394).
