$DATUM Boc-Dab(Cbz)-Gly-OtBu (62). To a solution of the acid 61 (1.00 g, 2.84
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (20 mL) at 0 ºC was added glycine tert-butyl ester (0.71
g, 4.26 mmol), NMM (0.94 mL, 8.52 mmol), HOBt (0.46 g, 3.41 mmol), and
EDC (0.65 g, 3.41 mmol). Reaction mixture was then slowly allowed to warm
to rt. After stirring overnight at rt, the mixture was concentrated. The
residue was taken up in EtOAc and washed with 10% citric acid (2 × 30
mL), sat. NaHCO3 (2 × 30 mL) and brine. The EtOAc layer was dried over
Na2SO4 and the crude product obtained after evaporation of EtOAc was
purified by silica gel column chromatography to afford the dipeptide 62
(1.16 g, 88% yield) as oil. R f 0.45 (EtOAc/hexanes, 2:3); [α]D −5.4 (c
0.48, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.33–7.25 (m, 6H, Ar, NH), 5.69
(bs, 1H, NH), 5.54 (bs, 1H, NH), 5.12–5.00 (m, 2H, CH 2Ph), 4.26 (m, 1H,
α-CH), 3.99–3.76 (m, 2H, CH 2:Gly), 3.48, 3.09 (2m, 2H, γ-CH 2),
1.97–1.75 (m, 2H, β-CH 2), 1.45, 1.39 (2s, 18H, C(CH 3)3); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.0, 168.8 (C(=O)), 157.1, 155.9 (NHC(=O)O), 136.7,
128.6, 128.2 (C Ar), 82.4, 80.3 (C(CH3)3), 67.0 (OCH2Ph), 51.8 (α-C),
42.3 (CH 2), 37.6 (γ-C), 34.3 (β-C), 28.6, 28.4 (C(CH3)3); ESI-LRMS m/z
466.6 (M+H)+.
