$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl
2-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinamido)acetate (INT-A): HATU (0.36 g, 0.96
mmol) and DIPEA (0.25 mL, 1.4 mmol) were added to a solution of
4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic acid (0.27 g, 0.80 mmol) in DMF (2 mL). After
10 min, methyl 2-aminoacetate HCl salt (0.1 g, 0.80 mmol) was added. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. The mixture
was diluted with EtOAc, washed with brine, concentrated, and purified by
silica gel column chromatography (0-100% EtOAc in hexanes). (S)-Methyl
1-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinoyl)pyrrolidine-2-carboxylate: The title
compound was synthesized similarly to INT-A using (S)-methyl
pyrrolidine-2-carboxylate HCl salt (165 mg, 0.76 mmol) and
4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic acid (254 mg, 0.76 mmol). The reaction
mixture was diluted with EtOAc, washed with brine, concentrated and
purified by silica gel column chromatography (0-100% EtOAc in hexanes).
The product as a clear oil (298 mg, 88%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ
ppm 8.07-8.36 (m, 1 H) 7.51-7.69 (m, 1 H) 7.27-7.51 (m, 10 H) 5.24-5.38
(m, 4 H) 3.65 (s, 3 H) 3.58-3.64 (m, 1 H) 2.72-2.76 (m, 1 H) 2.65-2.72
(m, 1 H) 2.14-2.34 (m, 1 H) 1.74-1.96 (m, 3 H). ESI-MS m/z: 447.1 [M +
H]+.
