$DATUM Boc-D-Glu(OCH3)-Gly-OtBu (21). To an ice-cold CH2Cl2 (25 mL) solution of
Boc-Glutamic acid 5-methyl ester (20) (3.00 g, 11.48 mmol), HOBt ( 1.86
g, 13.77 mmol), EDC (2.64 g, 13.77 mmol), HCl.Gly-OtBu ( 2.88 g, 17.22
mmol) and NMM (3.78 mL, 34.44 mmol) were added and the reaction mixture
was allowed to warm to rt overnight. Then reaction mixture was diluted
with CH2Cl2 (20 mL) and washed consecutively with 10% citric acid
solution (30 mL), sat. NaHCO3 solution (2 × 20 mL) and brine; dried over
Na2SO4 and the residue obtained after evaporation of CH2Cl2 was purified
by column chromatography with 20% EtOAc/hexanes to isolate product as a
colorless oil. (3.78 g, 88% yield). R f 0.3 (EtOAc/hexanes, 1:2); [α]D
+4.5 (c 0.64, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.99 (s, 1H, NH), 5.51
(d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H, NH), 4.24–4.16 (m, 1H, α-CH:Glu), 3.92–3.75 (m, 2H,
CH 2:Gly), 3.59 (s, 3H, OCH 3), 2.48– 2.33 (m, 2H, γ-CH 2:Glu), 2.17–2.03
(m, 1H, β-CH AHB:Glu), 1.93–1.83 (m, 1H, β-CHA H B:Glu), 1.37, 1.35 (2s,
18H, C(CH 3)3); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.8, 171.9, 168.7 (C(=O)),
155.8 (C(=O)NH), 82.2, 80.1 (C(CH3)3), 53.8 (α-C:Glu), 51.9 (OCH3), 42.2
(CH2:Gly), 30.5 (γ-C:Glu), 28.6, 28.4 (C(CH3)3), 28.3 (β-C:Glu); ESI-HRMS
m/z 375.2148 (M+H)+, C17H30N2O7 + H+ requires 375.2131.
