$DATUM N-{3-[{3-[(1,4-Dioxido-1,2,4-benzotriazin-3-yl)amino]propyl}(methyl)amino]propyl}-5-methyl-4-acridinecarboxamide
(12). A solution of 5-methylacridine-4-carboxylic acid (27)30 (0.13 g,
0.55 mmol) and CDI (0.21 g, 1.3 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) was stirred at 55 °C
for 24 h. The solution was diluted with dry benzene (10 mL), Sephadex
LH-20 (300 mg) was added, and the mixture stirred at 20 °C for 1 h. The
mixture was filtered and the solvent evaporated. The residue was
dissolved in dry THF (5 mL), a solution of 21 (80 mg, 0.27 mmol) in THF
(5 mL) added, and the solution stirred at 20 °C for 70 h. The solvent was
evaporated and the residue purified by chromatography, eluting with a
gradient (0-2%) of aqueous NH3/(0-8%) MeOH/DCM, to give compound 12 (0.13
g, 88%) as a red powder: mp (DCM/pet. ether) 158-162 °C; 1H NMR δ 12.08
(br s, 1 H, CONH), 8.83 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1 H, ArH), 8.76 (s, 1 H, NH),
8.06 (t, J = 8.9 Hz, 2 H, ArH), 7.97 (br d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H, ArH), 7.83
(d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H, ArH), 7.66 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 1 H, ArH), 7.56-7.63 (m,
2 H, ArH), 7.46 (dd, J = 7.6, 6.5 Hz, 1 H, ArH), 7.30 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1
H, ArH), 3.77 (q, J = 6.3 Hz, 2 H, CH2), 4.80-4.85 (m, 2 H, CH2),
3.06-3.10 (m, 4 H, 2 × CH2), 2.83 (s, 3 H, CH3), 2.67 (br s, 3 H, CH3),
2.30-2.35 (m, 2 H, CH2), 2.13-2.17 (m, 2 H, CH2); 13C NMR δ 166.5, 149.6,
146.9, 145.1, 137.9 (2), 135.8, 135.3, 135.1, 132.4, 131.2, 130.0, 127.9,
126.8, 126.4, 126.3, 126.2, 125.8, 125.2, 121.3, 117.0, 55.1, 54.5, 40.5,
39.2, 37.4, 26.1, 24.5, 19.0; HRMS calcd for C29H32N7O3 (MH+) m/z
526.2593, found 526.2582. Anal. (C29H31N7O3•1/2H2O) C, H, N.
