$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Macrocycle Ester 27. To the DMF solution of 26 from the last step (~600
mL, 6.91 mmol, KF = 3000 ppm) was added diisopropylethylamine (48 mL,
27.2 mmol) slowly to control the reaction temperature at 2-5 °C with
cooling, and then the mixture was allowed to warm to 20 °C. In a separate
vessel, HATU (334 g, 8.5 mmol) was added followed by 760 mL of DMF. The
DMF solution of 26 was then added dropwise to the HATU solution at rt
with vigorous agitation over 2.4 h, and HPLC assay indicated complete
conversion. The reaction was cooled to 10 °C and added to a vessel
containing 135 mL water and 900 mL MTBE. The layers were cut, and the
aqueous layer was back-extracted with 400 mL MTBE, and the combined MTBE
layers were washed with 340 mL of 5% citric acid followed by 360 mL
brine. The organic layer was dried with Na2SO4 and solvent switched to
THF via distillation with 500 mL THF. A concentrated solution (93.3 g)
was obtained that contained 36.2 g of macrocycle 27 (88% overall yield
from 22), 94.7% purity. An analytically pure sample was obtained via
silica gel chromatography, and spectroscopic data were consistent with
literature.2a
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Sonogashira coupling reaction (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Practical Synthesis of A Macrocyclic HCV Protease Inhibitor: A
High-Yielding Macrolactam Formation
