$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of NHS Esters.
Method A:To a solution of carboxylic acid 40a-e and 40j-k, (1.0 mmol, 1.0
equiv) in THF (10 mL) at 0 °C were added N-hydroxysuccinimide (1.0 mmol,
1.0 equiv) and DCC (1.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv). The resulting mixture was
stirred for 30 min at 0 °C then 2 h at rt. The reaction mixture was
filtered to remove the DCU precipitate, and the filtrate was concentrated
under reduced pressure. Purification by flash chromatography afforded the
desired N-hydroxysuccinimdyl aroyl ester.
2̕,3̕-O,O-Bis(t-butyldimethylsilyl)-5̕-O-{N-[(cyclohexyl)-carbonyl]sulfamoyl}adenosine
Triethylammonium Salt (42g), yield 87%. Rf 0.22 (6:4 EtOAc/MeOH); 1H NMR
(600 MHz, CD3OD) δ -0.37 (s, 3H), -0.01 (s, 3H), 0.16 (s, 3H), 0.17 (s,
3H), 0.71 (s, 9H), 0.98 (s, 9H), 1.23 (t, J =7.2 Hz, 9H), 1.28-1.33 (m,
3H), 1.43-1.46 (m, 2H), 1.65- 1.66 (m, 1H), 1.75-1.76 (m, 2H), 1.86-1.88
(m, 2H), 2.16 (tt, J =11.4, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 3.06 (q, J =7.2 Hz, 6H),
4.30-4.33 (m, 3H), 4.45 (d, J =4.2 Hz, 1H), 4.84-4.86 (m, 1H, obscured by
CD3OD: assigned by gCOSY as H-2̕), 6.11 (d, J =7.8 Hz, 1H), 8.18 (s, 1H),
8.56 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CD3OD) δ -5.3, -4.33, -4.28 (2C), 9.7,
18.6, 18.9, 26.2, 26.4, 27.0, 27.4, 31.25, 31.29, 47.6, 69.0, 74.9, 77.5,
86.4, 88.2, 120.1, 141.5, 151.1, 153.9, 157.3, 185.8; MS (ESI-) calcd for
C29H51N6O7SSi2 [M - H]- 683.3, found 683.3.
