$DATUM A solution of the carboxylic acid (6.0 g, 23.5 mmol),
N,O-dimethylhydroxylamine hydrochloride (3.0 g, 30.5 mmol),
4-(dimethylamino)pyridine (2.9 g, 23.5 mmol), and
N-ethyl-N'-[3-(dimethylamino)propyl]carbodiimide hydrochloride (EDCI, 4.5
g, 23.5 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (70 mL) was stirred for 3 h at rt under Ar. The
solution was washed with hydrochloric acid (pH 2) until the pH of the
aqueous layer was acidic. The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4. After
concentration, the residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexanes/acetone 10:1 to 2:1) to afford the Weinreb amide.
trans-3-[5-(Benzyloxy)-3-pyridyl]-N-methoxy-N-methylacrylamide, white
solid, yield 6.0 g, 86%. Mp 87-90 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.37 (m, 2H),
7.67 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 7.44-7.32 (m, 6H), 7.05 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H),
5.13 (s, 2H), 3.75 (s, 3H), 3.30 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 166.3,
155.1, 142.4, 139.8, 139.3, 136.0, 131.7, 128.9, 128.6, 127.7, 119.8,
118.4, 70.7, 62.2, 32.7; MS (ESI) m/z 299.1 (M+H+).
